      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Actually, electrons do not physically flow from one plate to the other through the insulating dielectric material inside the capacitor. Instead, current appears to flow because the external charging and discharging cycle causes electrons to accumulate on one plate and deplete from the other. This movement of charge at the surface creates a continuous conduction current in the connected wires, even though no electrons cross the gap between the plates themselves. Think of it like a hydraulic system where water sloshes back and forth in tanks rather than flowing through a pipe between them.",
