      "role": "user",
      "content": "ok i get the water analogy. but if there is a literal gap and nothing is crossing it, what is actually \"pushing\" the electrons to move back and forth like that? is it just the voltage changing, or is there some kind of internal force or field interaction that keeps it moving in sync with the frequency?",
