      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The changing electric field between the plates creates a non-conservative induced electromotive force (EMF) that acts like a pump, continuously pushing electrons in and out of the nearby wires. This isn't about a single internal force on the electrons; rather, the alternating voltage source drives the local electric field at each plate, causing the surface charge distribution to shift in sync with the signal frequency. Essentially, whatever mechanism moves the source electrons toward the plate increases the local field, which in turn accelerates new electrons toward the opposite plate to maintain continuity in the circuit.",
